{
 "title": "The Curtains",
 "rule_text": "After dark every curtain in town is closed, and nobody looks outside.",
 "tell": "curtains",
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In this town, every curtain is closed before sunset.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody looks outside after dark. Nobody.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "At dusk, every house on our street pulls its curtains shut.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Even the Mayor, with his big top hat, shakes while he closes his.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "I'm Sam, and I always obey. Mom does too.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mom wears her red cardigan, the one missing a button.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "She hums while she cooks. Every single night.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "My sister Lily taps her spoon three times before eating.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "But one night, Mom thought I wasn't home yet.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "She was worried. She stepped to our window.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Slowly, she pulled the curtains open. Just a tiny slit.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Far across the street, something tall stood in the dark.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two glowing eyes. Looking straight back at her.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mom's face went white. She yanked the curtains closed.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "I was upstairs. I saw nothing. I heard nothing.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "The next day, we sat down for dinner.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mom smiled at me before I even finished talking.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "She set a fourth plate, for nobody at all.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lily asked for the salt. Mom said it a beat late.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "The kitchen was silent. Mom wasn't humming.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "I stared at her. She never blinked. Not once.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lily tapped her spoon three times. Mom tapped it eleven.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Her smile stretched wider. Too wide. Way too wide.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "And her cardigan had every button. Every single one.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "That was never Mom. The curtains never kept it out.",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "They just kept us from seeing it. Then it smiled and said,",
   "speaker": "narrator"
  },
  {
   "text": "Eat your dinner, sweetie... and don't look outside.",
   "speaker": "mimic"
  }
 ],
 "both_stages": true,
 "notes": "- Row 1 (the hook): stage B, me on seat_back (sitting, the closed curtains right behind me), camera close, facing the camera, time dinner.\n- The dusk line: stage A, time sunset, camera street, props.curtains 'closing'; then our house (a wide or medium with me / Mom on the porch) with curtains 'closing'.\n- The Mayor: stage A, mayor on win_mayor, camera window, pose hold_up2 (his arm up, pulling the curtain), face scared, props.curtains 'closing', time sunset.\n- Mom's peek: stage A night: mom on win_ours, camera window, props.peek true (curtains closed with a slit), face worried. Then her view: camera pov, subject ['creature'], the creature on cr_across facing {to: win_ours}. Then back to mom on win_ours, camera window, face terrified (one of the two big shock faces) with push 0.15.\n- Me safe inside: stage B, time dinner_cold, me on stand_kitchen or a seat, not seeing it.\n- The dinner: stage B: mimic on seat_back (the closed curtains behind her), me on seat_left, sister on seat_right; seat_front is the empty place (insert plate_front for a place set for nobody). Warm (dinner) at first, dinner_cold as it gets wrong.\n- The smile (the last big moment): mimic on seat_back, camera close, face mimic_wide (the too-wide smile, only here), facing camera, push 0.2, held over the line; the last line may stay on it or cut to me.\n- Night rows on stage A: the engine closes every curtain by itself (leave props.curtains out, or say closed).",
